WEBVTT

00:00:01.520 --> 00:00:03.810
The jamming signals are going full blast.

00:00:03.810 --> 00:00:06.560
There's no way for us to contact
the Coyote like this.

00:00:06.860 --> 00:00:09.400
We'll just have to go down there.

00:00:09.530 --> 00:00:12.240
How much time left before the bomb goes off?

00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:15.910
As much time as we've got left to live, maybe.

00:00:16.410 --> 00:00:18.160
Are you still gonna go?

00:00:18.410 --> 00:00:19.540
With pleasure!

00:00:19.910 --> 00:00:22.290
So do we stop the bomb first...

00:00:22.290 --> 00:00:25.080
Or take back Bruce's legacy first?

00:00:40.390 --> 00:00:43.690
Distance to Gigabanks: 6300.

00:00:43.690 --> 00:00:45.400
That ain't too far.

00:01:22.850 --> 00:01:26.230
I etch out today with my finger

00:01:26.230 --> 00:01:29.610
on the dusty hood of a car

00:01:29.610 --> 00:01:33.110
As the rain shower passed over

00:01:33.110 --> 00:01:35.950
it vanished just like love

00:01:36.070 --> 00:01:43.160
There's something in your heart you can't get rid of

00:01:43.160 --> 00:01:49.830
So beat your invisible wings

00:01:49.830 --> 00:01:53.630
We'll fight back against the wind

00:01:53.630 --> 00:01:56.550
that gusts at us so relentlessly

00:01:56.880 --> 00:01:59.970
We'll stand firm against it

00:01:59.970 --> 00:02:03.770
with steadfast emotion! Go!

00:02:03.770 --> 00:02:10.690
We continue running on our way

00:02:10.690 --> 00:02:16.690
to a place promised, where sandstorms whirl

00:02:16.690 --> 00:02:19.820
Tonight is the night

00:02:20.320 --> 00:02:23.330
We're gonna make it through

00:02:23.490 --> 00:02:31.040
On to our destination

00:02:57.030 --> 00:03:01.030
Look! There is no truth behind
the Federation's words!

00:03:01.030 --> 00:03:03.660
This incident is further proof!

00:03:01.530 --> 00:03:08.450
Episode 10    Angelica Burns

00:03:03.660 --> 00:03:06.410
The mere thought of destroying an entire planet is a reprehensible act in and of itself,

00:03:06.410 --> 00:03:10.960
but that did not stop them from using it
as material for negotiations!

00:03:10.960 --> 00:03:13.210
What's more, it was all a lie in the first place!

00:03:13.210 --> 00:03:18.090
I believe you now understand how
degenerate the Federation is.

00:03:18.630 --> 00:03:23.220
We of the Graceland Liberation Forces 
have just launched a massive offensive,

00:03:23.220 --> 00:03:26.560
and I hereby declare once again that 
we are continuing our battle of Truth

00:03:26.560 --> 00:03:29.430
and we will accomplish our mission!

00:03:31.770 --> 00:03:33.440
Morale Rises Among the Graceland Liberation Forces {Sign}

00:03:32.810 --> 00:03:35.900
Colonel Richard of the Liberation Forces
has made his statement as you have just seen,

00:03:35.900 --> 00:03:38.150
and combat between the two sides has resumed.

00:03:38.280 --> 00:03:41.820
Please have a look at the video we
just received from the front.

00:03:48.950 --> 00:03:55.040
Hostilities seem to be escalating, with the area
around Godwing experiencing the fiercest fighting.

00:03:52.250 --> 00:03:55.630
File Footage

00:03:55.040 --> 00:03:56.960
Upon hearing Colonel Richard's speech,

00:03:55.630 --> 00:03:59.630
Federation Forces

00:03:55.630 --> 00:03:59.630
G-land Liberation Forces

00:03:56.960 --> 00:03:59.590
the Liberation Forces 
have launched an all-out offensive.

00:03:59.590 --> 00:04:01.170
Now I'd like to go back and reexamine
the scene of the "photonic bomb explosion"

00:04:01.170 --> 00:04:04.090
<i>Now I'd like to go back and reexamine
the scene of the "photonic bomb explosion"</i>

00:04:01.300 --> 00:04:04.090
So the photonic bomb was a bluff?

00:04:04.090 --> 00:04:08.890
Well, then, it seems we can settle down 
and search for Bruce's treasure at our own pace.

00:04:04.090 --> 00:04:05.470
<i>-which is so key here,</i>

00:04:05.470 --> 00:04:07.260
<i>-with our military analyst, Mr. Yamaguchi.</i>

00:04:07.430 --> 00:04:08.890
<i>-Please go ahead, Mr. Yamaguchi.</i>

00:04:08.890 --> 00:04:10.060
<i>-Thank you.</i>

00:04:09.430 --> 00:04:11.140
I wonder about that.

00:04:10.430 --> 00:04:14.150
<i>-We can only conclude that the bomb was a fake.</i>

00:04:11.680 --> 00:04:14.150
Is there something that's got you concerned?

00:04:14.150 --> 00:04:16.730
No, I wouldn't say that.

00:04:14.270 --> 00:04:15.770
<i>-It was a ruse.</i>

00:04:17.690 --> 00:04:22.030
Well, it is too bad for us that they couldn't have
carried on their war a little farther away though,

00:04:22.030 --> 00:04:24.990
since they're right on the spot we're after.

00:04:27.080 --> 00:04:28.450
How is May doing?

00:04:29.120 --> 00:04:33.460
She should be up and about just like
normal in about half a day.

00:04:52.020 --> 00:04:54.390
What the hell is going on here anyway?!

00:04:54.390 --> 00:04:56.560
Yeah, this is pretty weird.

00:04:56.560 --> 00:05:02.940
I thought they were saying up until yesterday that
there was a cease-fire on account of the bomb.

00:05:03.150 --> 00:05:04.950
Something happened...

00:05:05.450 --> 00:05:07.120
Any word from Bishop?

00:05:07.120 --> 00:05:08.320
Nothing.

00:05:08.320 --> 00:05:11.700
The signal's been on the whole time, but...

00:05:20.800 --> 00:05:22.300
February?

00:05:22.300 --> 00:05:24.340
<i>What is it, Mother?</i>

00:05:24.340 --> 00:05:27.300
Have you received word from April?

00:05:27.300 --> 00:05:29.350
<i>No, not yet.</i>

00:05:31.010 --> 00:05:35.770
Please bring the inspector who
was with May to my quarters.

00:05:36.100 --> 00:05:37.650
<i>Yes, Mother.</i>

00:05:48.450 --> 00:05:51.660
I don't know anything about the photonic bomb.

00:05:51.660 --> 00:05:57.040
In fact, this is the first I've heard of the photonic
bomb aboard the Jupiter being a fake.

00:06:02.090 --> 00:06:04.510
Listen, I've got a question for you.

00:06:05.920 --> 00:06:07.340
Go ahead.

00:06:07.340 --> 00:06:11.510
What is this treasure that you 
and Mister are both searching for?

00:06:12.720 --> 00:06:15.230
My, where did that come from?

00:06:16.730 --> 00:06:19.060
Do you have an interest in it?

00:06:19.060 --> 00:06:24.070
I want to know what would make you come to
Graceland at a time like this.

00:06:24.070 --> 00:06:30.490
Or rather, I want to know what it is that would make
Mister defy such danger to come here.

00:06:35.620 --> 00:06:37.080
Money, my dear.

00:06:38.080 --> 00:06:43.250
I'm telling you that it's money that would make
Mister defy danger to come here.

00:06:44.800 --> 00:06:45.960
I see.

00:06:45.960 --> 00:06:50.260
I imagine he may even be digging up dirt
on Graceland right about now.

00:06:50.760 --> 00:06:53.350
Then Mister is here?

00:06:55.520 --> 00:06:57.850
Are you sure it's okay for you to be so laid back?

00:06:57.850 --> 00:07:02.400
If it's the Mister I know, he may have
already reached the treasure.

00:07:02.400 --> 00:07:04.270
Angelica!

00:07:05.650 --> 00:07:07.240
There's one other thing.

00:07:06.820 --> 00:07:08.900
Come on, Angelica!

00:07:08.860 --> 00:07:10.410
Is May all right?

00:07:12.910 --> 00:07:14.280
Yes...

00:07:15.240 --> 00:07:16.410
That's good.

00:07:18.710 --> 00:07:21.580
It's not good at all!

00:07:21.920 --> 00:07:25.710
After this, I'm sure they'll execute us or hang us!

00:07:25.710 --> 00:07:29.130
NO!

00:07:38.270 --> 00:07:39.480
Let's go.

00:08:14.720 --> 00:08:16.180
Are you all right?

00:08:16.350 --> 00:08:18.310
What about you?

00:08:39.200 --> 00:08:42.460
We might have known security would
be this tight at the entrance.

00:08:43.460 --> 00:08:44.670
Ready to do it?

00:08:44.460 --> 00:08:45.330
Yeah!

00:08:54.340 --> 00:08:55.890
All set?

00:08:55.890 --> 00:08:56.720
Sure.

00:08:56.720 --> 00:08:57.680
Yeah!

00:09:03.140 --> 00:09:04.600
Hey, Mister.

00:09:04.600 --> 00:09:07.230
We're screwed if they see you.
Keep your head down.

00:09:07.230 --> 00:09:09.360
But something's weird here!

00:09:09.360 --> 00:09:12.150
It seems like we're not headed
in the right direction.

00:09:12.150 --> 00:09:14.530
Maybe we should go farther in.

00:09:17.200 --> 00:09:19.120
All right, keep yourself hidden.

00:09:19.120 --> 00:09:20.200
Right.

00:09:44.390 --> 00:09:46.060
We made it by somehow.

00:09:59.280 --> 00:10:01.080
Hey! You think this is it?

00:10:04.870 --> 00:10:06.410
We're heading around to the final curve.

00:10:06.410 --> 00:10:08.960
We're about to make a comeback
at the very last second!

00:10:08.960 --> 00:10:12.210
If Bishop were here now he'd tell
you not to be too hasty.

00:10:16.050 --> 00:10:18.680
<i>This is Bishop. Do you read me, Mister?</i>

00:10:18.680 --> 00:10:20.430
It's Bishop!

00:10:24.100 --> 00:10:27.190
<i>Bishop, this is Franca. Do you read me?</i>

00:10:27.190 --> 00:10:28.810
Yeah, I read you.

00:10:28.810 --> 00:10:29.850
Is everyone all right?

00:10:29.850 --> 00:10:31.310
<i>Of course!</i>

00:10:31.310 --> 00:10:32.520
What about the treasure?

00:10:32.820 --> 00:10:35.190
We're about to go down into the cave now.

00:10:35.610 --> 00:10:37.610
<i>I see, is Mister there?</i>

00:10:37.780 --> 00:10:39.410
Yeah, I'll put him on.

00:10:39.410 --> 00:10:40.200
Mister?

00:10:40.950 --> 00:10:42.280
Did it go all right?

00:10:42.580 --> 00:10:45.700
I'd like to say yeah, but things
have gotten pretty bad.

00:10:47.000 --> 00:10:48.670
Yeah...

00:10:48.670 --> 00:10:50.960
Yeah, yeah...

00:10:51.130 --> 00:10:54.000
All right. Okay, we'll be waiting for you.

00:10:54.000 --> 00:10:55.710
We'll hook up with you aftewvards.

00:10:55.880 --> 00:10:57.010
What's up, Mister?

00:10:57.010 --> 00:10:58.420
Did he blow it?

00:10:58.420 --> 00:11:00.260
Nah, it's not that.

00:11:00.260 --> 00:11:01.760
That's not what happened,

00:11:01.760 --> 00:11:07.060
but what it all amounts to is that the bomb is
counting down to detonation even as we speak.

00:11:07.270 --> 00:11:09.020
What are you talking about?

00:11:09.020 --> 00:11:12.520
Apparently, the photonic bomb aboard
the Jupiter was just a bluff.

00:11:12.520 --> 00:11:17.240
It sounds like the real photonic bomb is buried
somewhere beneath Godwing here.

00:11:17.240 --> 00:11:18.280
Huh?!

00:11:18.280 --> 00:11:24.120
What's more, the Liberation Forces don't know
that the real photonic bomb is buried here,

00:11:24.120 --> 00:11:27.250
so they think that the bombing
has been suspended too.

00:11:27.250 --> 00:11:29.870
So, that's why the fighting resumed.

00:11:29.870 --> 00:11:34.920
So this planet really is going to
explode in less than a day?!

00:11:35.420 --> 00:11:39.800
We're the only ones who know that the
other photonic bomb was a bluff.

00:11:40.050 --> 00:11:45.050
I don't feel the need to worry about people
who have willingly chosen to die,

00:11:45.050 --> 00:11:49.180
but the fact that we're the only ones who
know puts us in a pretty lousy position.

00:11:49.560 --> 00:11:52.730
This is one hell of a thing you've left us with, Bruce.

00:11:53.400 --> 00:11:55.320
<i>Heh, I'll bet you're getting a kick out of it.</i>

00:11:56.730 --> 00:11:59.530
I know what you're thinking, you old bastard.

00:11:59.990 --> 00:12:02.320
<i>Take care of Franca for me, man.</i>

00:12:06.620 --> 00:12:07.910
Ready to go?

00:12:07.910 --> 00:12:08.750
Sure!

00:12:42.650 --> 00:12:43.910
Mister?

00:12:44.530 --> 00:12:46.780
It's definitely ahead.

00:12:46.780 --> 00:12:50.870
Maybe the effects of the war have eroded
the strength of the ground.

00:12:50.950 --> 00:12:52.870
Then Gigabanks might also be...

00:12:52.870 --> 00:12:56.380
We won't know that until we get there.

00:12:56.380 --> 00:12:57.790
Let's backtrack a bit.

00:12:57.790 --> 00:13:02.550
There was a side passage back there, and I'll bet
it hooks back up somewhere along the line.

00:13:04.010 --> 00:13:07.140
Send August to assist January.

00:13:07.140 --> 00:13:09.060
June's squad move to sector B-8.

00:13:09.060 --> 00:13:11.270
March, you go to sector G-S.

00:13:11.430 --> 00:13:16.400
And communicate to all troops that we will continue
on course with our operation tonight.

00:13:16.400 --> 00:13:19.730
We will continue our search until
Gigabanks is located.

00:13:20.070 --> 00:13:21.730
What's the matter?

00:13:21.730 --> 00:13:25.200
You're acting as if this were our last day.

00:13:26.780 --> 00:13:28.490
I don't know...

00:13:28.490 --> 00:13:32.080
Or rather, I don't know,
but that is what I am thinking.

00:13:40.500 --> 00:13:42.800
It doesn't feel like my own body.

00:13:51.220 --> 00:13:53.180
It looks like we can go from here.

00:14:11.530 --> 00:14:12.450
C'mon.

00:14:19.670 --> 00:14:22.960
This is a dead end. Head back.

00:14:25.010 --> 00:14:27.380
That was our signal to get moving, wasn't it?

00:14:27.380 --> 00:14:29.140
Most likely. What do we do?

00:14:29.140 --> 00:14:31.390
Let's go, there's no time.

00:14:31.390 --> 00:14:34.720
I'm sure that Mister will figure out
a way to get back to us.

00:14:34.720 --> 00:14:36.060
Okay then, let's go.

00:15:07.130 --> 00:15:10.840
It sounds like that detective woman defied Mother.

00:15:10.840 --> 00:15:12.260
Detective?

00:15:12.260 --> 00:15:14.760
The sassy broad that was on Sandvil.

00:15:14.760 --> 00:15:16.680
Oh, that detective!

00:15:16.680 --> 00:15:17.890
Angelica?!

00:15:17.520 --> 00:15:18.520
Did they kill her?

00:15:18.640 --> 00:15:20.100
It sounds like she's still alive.

00:15:20.100 --> 00:15:21.940
Angelica is here?!

00:15:21.730 --> 00:15:23.110
Oh, too bad.

00:15:23.110 --> 00:15:25.320
Ten hours left...

00:15:25.320 --> 00:15:27.690
I can't just leave her where she is.

00:15:27.690 --> 00:15:28.700
Damn it!

00:15:31.820 --> 00:15:34.950
Should be all right now. Let's go!

00:15:39.620 --> 00:15:42.130
What's going on, Angelica?

00:15:42.130 --> 00:15:44.210
You don't want to be killed in
a place like this, do you?

00:15:44.210 --> 00:15:47.420
Well, no... But how are we gonna get out?

00:15:48.210 --> 00:15:49.800
A detective is always prepared.

00:15:58.890 --> 00:15:59.850
Hurry!

00:15:59.850 --> 00:16:01.100
Right!

00:16:07.480 --> 00:16:08.280
May!

00:16:07.980 --> 00:16:09.280
Your body...

00:16:09.280 --> 00:16:10.450
Not this way.

00:16:10.450 --> 00:16:12.030
Go that way instead.

00:16:12.030 --> 00:16:12.910
Thanks!

00:16:12.910 --> 00:16:14.450
See ya!

00:16:18.160 --> 00:16:20.460
I hope you're able to find Mister.

00:16:28.000 --> 00:16:29.760
This way no good either?

00:16:29.760 --> 00:16:30.720
Let's head back.

00:16:30.720 --> 00:16:35.720
We might find a side tunnel or something that will
take us to the other side of that first path.

00:16:35.720 --> 00:16:37.260
Okay, let's look for it.

00:16:37.260 --> 00:16:38.810
{We won't give up!}"Don't give up!" they say.

00:16:38.810 --> 00:16:40.680
Okay!

00:16:44.850 --> 00:16:46.980
Stay alive, Angelica!

00:16:53.570 --> 00:16:54.860
Angelica!

00:17:00.200 --> 00:17:02.830
Gal's got spunk! I'll be damned.

00:17:11.880 --> 00:17:12.880
Angelica!

00:17:12.880 --> 00:17:14.800
Keep quiet, you'll bite your tongue.

00:17:14.800 --> 00:17:15.760
M'kay!

00:17:39.780 --> 00:17:42.330
Angelica, get in! Hurry!

00:17:43.410 --> 00:17:44.210
Chelsea!

00:17:44.210 --> 00:17:45.370
Right!

00:17:45.710 --> 00:17:48.250
Angelica, you get in the back with me
and help fight them off.

00:17:48.250 --> 00:17:49.040
Okay...

00:17:48.750 --> 00:17:50.670
And the other girl there can drive.

00:17:50.670 --> 00:17:51.460
Roger!

00:18:11.230 --> 00:18:12.570
You wanna die?!

00:18:21.740 --> 00:18:22.580
They're here!

00:18:23.790 --> 00:18:24.870
Sons of bitches...

00:18:50.360 --> 00:18:51.730
Last one!

00:19:12.880 --> 00:19:14.210
Why?

00:19:14.420 --> 00:19:16.630
Why did you come to my rescue?

00:19:16.880 --> 00:19:19.180
Hey, why not?

00:19:19.180 --> 00:19:22.510
See, I heard an acquaintance of mine
had come all this way.

00:19:22.510 --> 00:19:25.100
Figured I'd just come say hi real quick.

00:19:29.890 --> 00:19:31.650
Was I intruding?

00:19:32.520 --> 00:19:34.070
No, not at all.

00:19:41.820 --> 00:19:43.160
But y'know...

00:19:43.160 --> 00:19:46.120
I can't afford to take it slow.

00:19:47.200 --> 00:19:51.710
Pretty soon, the photonic bomb is gonna detonate
and this planet will be toast.

00:19:52.080 --> 00:19:54.710
But the photonic bomb was a lie!

00:19:54.710 --> 00:19:57.630
Nope, I don't got the time to explain.

00:19:57.630 --> 00:20:03.550
All I can say is that, in less than ten hours,
this planet really is gonna vanish.

00:20:03.550 --> 00:20:04.720
That's a lie!

00:20:04.720 --> 00:20:06.390
If you leave now, you can still make it.

00:20:06.390 --> 00:20:08.980
Take that younger gal with you and get outta here.

00:20:08.980 --> 00:20:10.850
But... But...

00:20:10.850 --> 00:20:12.810
Get outta here!

00:20:12.810 --> 00:20:16.070
What are... What are you going to do?

00:20:16.070 --> 00:20:20.200
I'll stay here, 'cuz there's still stuff left for me to do.

00:20:20.200 --> 00:20:22.360
If you're going to stay here, then I will too!

00:20:37.250 --> 00:20:40.220
If you're going to stay here, then I will too.

00:20:40.220 --> 00:20:43.720
Because it's my job to capture you.

00:20:45.470 --> 00:20:46.970
Perfect.

00:20:55.730 --> 00:20:58.480
If your job is to capture me,

00:20:58.480 --> 00:21:01.780
then as a policewoman, it's also your job
to save lives. Am I right?

00:21:02.820 --> 00:21:10.330
There's pretty much no one on this planet who
knows that it's set to explode right on schedule.

00:21:11.000 --> 00:21:15.710
I don't give a damn about what happens to these
assholes blowing each other away without a care,

00:21:15.710 --> 00:21:19.840
but it would be pretty sad if the people who weren't
like that just went "boom" all of a sudden.

00:21:19.840 --> 00:21:25.550
I want you to try and get as many civilians
as possible off the planet.

00:21:26.300 --> 00:21:29.760
What are you staying here for?

00:21:30.060 --> 00:21:33.640
Coyotes won't betray their kin,
even if it costs them their lives!

00:21:33.640 --> 00:21:37.060
There are some folks on this planet
who are still waiting for me.

00:21:37.060 --> 00:21:38.820
I've gotta go to them.

00:21:38.820 --> 00:21:42.650
I... l...

00:21:44.950 --> 00:21:47.820
I'm no good at the romantic stuff.

00:21:57.790 --> 00:22:00.000
All right, girl, switch with me.

00:22:00.000 --> 00:22:01.840
All right!

00:22:28.030 --> 00:22:29.410
Let's move!

00:22:39.420 --> 00:22:43.170
<i>Where are these waterdrops</i>

00:22:43.210 --> 00:22:52.970
<i>that travel along my cheek coming from?</i>

00:22:53.930 --> 00:22:58.770
<i>Tell me...</i>

00:23:00.560 --> 00:23:11.530
<i>I grabbed the rule that says we can't turn back time</i>

00:23:11.530 --> 00:23:18.540
<i>by the collar</i>

00:23:19.250 --> 00:23:22.880
<i>I resist the fading memories</i>

00:23:22.880 --> 00:23:33.140
<i>even with the feelings here</i>

00:23:33.260 --> 00:23:37.140
<i>But I'm sure they'll come to kill me</i>

00:23:37.310 --> 00:23:43.230
<i>From out of all the days that have gone by</i>

00:23:43.270 --> 00:23:51.820
<i>there's only one thing I can believe in</i>

00:23:51.820 --> 00:23:58.120
<i>I cried until my voice was hoarse</i>

00:23:58.120 --> 00:24:01.580
<i>Come to me</i>

00:24:01.790 --> 00:24:04.880
<i>Be by my side</i>

00:24:04.880 --> 00:24:09.220
<i>O Kay?</i>
